{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1541723-ideas-on-how-supernaturals-respond-to-the-rite-of-investment","id":1541723,"title":"Ideas on how supernaturals respond to the Rite of Investment","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-07T23:16:51-07:00","id":1541723,"title":"Ideas on how supernaturals respond to the Rite of Investment","content":"Hello everyone!<br /> <br /> Today I'm asking for ideas on how various kinds of supernaturals might respond to the Rite of Investment compared to Immortals and Ephemeral Entities (whose response to the Rite is already detailed in Book of Lasting Death), particularly if I decide to run a crossover adventure where all PCs are invested cultists or Arisen, but they can be from other lines, like vampires, werewolves, etc. I'm using the 2nd edition rules. <br /> <br /> Thank you for your help!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T23:03:12-07:00","id":1541763,"title":"","content":"In the Chronicle i m running the Mummy invested a Promethean, i decided as a side effect that when the Promethean would cause Disquiet he instead cause the correspondent level of Sybaris","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T00:27:14-07:00","id":1541765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1541723-ideas-on-how-supernaturals-respond-to-the-rite-of-investment?p=1541763#post1541763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Chronicle i m running the Mummy invested a Promethean, i decided as a side effect that when the Promethean would cause Disquiet he instead cause the correspondent level of Sybaris</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that. It makes things easier for the Promethean, right? I understand Disquiet to be worse than Sybaris, though there are similarities between the two. Also, cultists with Scorpion Cult Initiation 2 are immune to Sybaris, which would allow the Promethean to be around a certain group of humans indefinitely... Surely a welcome change and a good motivation to join a mummy's cult.<br /> Do you allow him the use of Affinities or Utterances? How many points can the Arisen invest? I would imagine he would be comparable to an Immortal (4 Pillar points max, access to master's decree Affinities and level 1 Utterances), although for Ephemeral Cultists the max points depend on their Rank and they don't get access to Affinities or Utterances, only some specific advantages depending on what they are (spirit, ghost, shade, goetia, fiend, etc.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T10:36:47-07:00","id":1541786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1541723-ideas-on-how-supernaturals-respond-to-the-rite-of-investment?p=1541765#post1541765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like that. It makes things easier for the Promethean, right? I understand Disquiet to be worse than Sybaris, though there are similarities between the two. Also, cultists with Scorpion Cult Initiation 2 are immune to Sybaris, which would allow the Promethean to be around a certain group of humans indefinitely... Surely a welcome change and a good motivation to join a mummy's cult.<br /> Do you allow him the use of Affinities or Utterances? How many points can the Arisen invest? I would imagine he would be comparable to an Immortal (4 Pillar points max, access to master's decree Affinities and level 1 Utterances), although for Ephemeral Cultists the max points depend on their Rank and they don't get access to Affinities or Utterances, only some specific advantages depending on what they are (spirit, ghost, shade, goetia, fiend, etc.).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they are surely similar but i think that the Promethean feels it as an &quot;alien&quot; intrusion in his Azoth.<br /> Also, as the Sybaris is centered on the Mummy overlord, all the cult member are immune to his specific Sybaris.<br /> Anyway, i think that the lack of Sekhem doesn t allow the Promethean to use Utterance or Affinities (except the Master decree affinity), i simply allow him to store a maximum of 4 pillar points, as an immortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T12:10:10-07:00","id":1541792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1541723-ideas-on-how-supernaturals-respond-to-the-rite-of-investment?p=1541786#post1541786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, they are surely similar but i think that the Promethean feels it as an &quot;alien&quot; intrusion in his Azoth.<br /> Also, as the Sybaris is centered on the Mummy overlord, all the cult member are immune to his specific Sybaris.<br /> Anyway, i think that the lack of Sekhem doesn t allow the Promethean to use Utterance or Affinities (except the Master decree affinity), i simply allow him to store a maximum of 4 pillar points, as an immortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think characters with 2+ dots in Scorpion Cult Initiation are immune to Sybaris from all sources, not only from their Arisen master, rules as written (2nd ed). Unless you decided to change it for your game, which is fine.<br /> <br /> Now you've made me curious to read the Promethean manual and develop my own crossover rules...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I'm thinking: can the Pillars of the soul be compared to the humours of Promethean the Created, to devise more specific benefits of being an Inheritor than just Mortal Decree? Shades for example get to manifest or materialise (can't remember exactly) from any shadow large enough to contain them; other ephemeral entities receive each a specific benefit. Prometheans are not mortals to my understanding, so Mortal Decree could be replaced by a more fitting benefit... (crazy thinking sounds)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16965,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","user":"Hermeticus","date":". 09-09-2024, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T12:21:45-07:00","id":1541793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1541723-ideas-on-how-supernaturals-respond-to-the-rite-of-investment?p=1541792#post1541792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think characters with 2+ dots in Scorpion Cult Initiation are immune to Sybaris from all sources, not only from their Arisen master, rules as written (2nd ed). </div> </div> </div> </div>No no, you are right.<br /> What i m saying is that the Promethean cause Sybaris centered on the investing mummy, and if i understand it rightly even a novice is immune to the Sybarys of his Mummy master, so every member of the cult is immune to the altered Promethean &quot;Disquiet&quot; (very convenient for him)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T12:24:37-07:00","id":1541794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1541723-ideas-on-how-supernaturals-respond-to-the-rite-of-investment?p=1541792#post1541792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now you've made me curious to read the Promethean manual and develop my own crossover rules...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I'm thinking: can the Pillars of the soul be compared to the humours of Promethean the Created, to devise more specific benefits of being an Inheritor than just Mortal Decree? Shades for example get to manifest or materialise (can't remember exactly) from any shadow large enough to contain them; other ephemeral entities receive each a specific benefit. Prometheans are not mortals to my understanding, so Mortal Decree could be replaced by a more fitting benefit... (crazy thinking sounds)</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Dark eras 2 book there is a sidebar that compares the Fivefold Pillars to the Promethean Universal Milestones.<br /> If you want to homebrew something that could be a good starting point<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T15:16:11-07:00","id":1541805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1541723-ideas-on-how-supernaturals-respond-to-the-rite-of-investment?p=1541794#post1541794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the Dark eras 2 book there is a sidebar that compares the Fivefold Pillars to the Promethean Universal Milestones.<br /> If you want to homebrew something that could be a good starting point<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I'm going to check it out, in sha Allah. I was thinking more in terms of the humours, but I don't know PtC well, so the Milestones are probably a better fit if the authors of Dark Eras opted for that.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I just looked Universal Milestones up and yes, they make a better fit because they are steps to become human and <i>gain a soul</i>, which in Arisen terms is made up of Pillars. And the link between some Milestones and certain Pillars is easy to spot.<br /> Humours would rather be correspondences of the soul's Pillars in the body (which is not far from real world classic philosophical and alchemic thought), though Prometheans have the peculiar condition of having them without a soul.<br /> I think it would be possible to allow the use of Pillar points to do something positive in relation to the corresponding Humour and Universal Milestone - what exactly depends on PtC's system and what would make sense in it, but it would provide extra motivation for Prometheans to join Arisen cults.<br /> <br /> Let's also remember that the Mesen-Nebu are alchemists among other things. I can see them cooperating with Prometheans and seeing the latter's Great Work as a process related to dweden. And the Osiris lineage is always easy to connect to mummies, perhaps a cultist's experiment during the first Sothic Turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16965,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","user":"Hermeticus","date":". 09-09-2024, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T16:13:37-07:00","id":1541812,"title":"","content":"<b>Vampire Inheritors</b><br /> Vampires can be invested with up to 4 Pillar points.<br /> <br /> When invested, they gain additional dots in a Discipline (which also counts towards the dice pools to activate the Discipline's powers) determined by the Arisen master's defining Pillar. The number of dots gained is equal to the Arisen's defining Pillar rating.<br /> <br /> A vampire does not gain extra powers for dots beyond 5 (between his own dots in it and those provided by the investment), but excess dots still apply as bonus to the dice pools to activate the Discipline's powers.<br /> <br /> Ab - Majesty<br /> Ba - Dominate<br /> Ka - Protean<br /> Ren - Auspex<br /> Sheut - Nightmare<br /> <br /> Example: Seti is an Ashem with Sheut 5. He invests 4 points from any Pillar in Phobos, a Nosferatu elder with Blood Potency 7. Phobos has Nightmare 3. Thanks to the investment he has effectively Nightmare 8. This means he can access the powers of Nightmare 4 and 5 which he did not know before, and adds 8 dice for Nightmare to his dice pools to activate the discipline's powers rather than 3 only.<br /> <br /> Using Discipline powers beyond those already known to the vampire (like Nightmare 4 and 5 in the example) costs 1 Pillar point per scene, in addition to other normal costs. <br /> <br /> If the Arisen reincarnates in the invested vampire's body (let's say it's possible), what happens? I want to avoid a weird vampire-mummy hybrid. Is the Beast cast out? What does that look like? Or does the Arisen need to fight the Beast psychically before taking over?<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16965,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","user":"Hermeticus","date":". 09-09-2024, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T03:53:09-07:00","id":1541844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1541723-ideas-on-how-supernaturals-respond-to-the-rite-of-investment?p=1541812#post1541812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Vampire Inheritors</b><br /> Vampires can be invested with up to 4 Pillar points.<br /> <br /> When invested, they gain additional dots in a Discipline (which also counts towards the dice pools to activate the Discipline's powers) determined by the Arisen master's defining Pillar. The number of dots gained is equal to the Arisen's defining Pillar rating.<br /> <br /> A vampire does not gain extra powers for dots beyond 5 (between his own dots in it and those provided by the investment), but excess dots still apply as bonus to the dice pools to activate the Discipline's powers.<br /> <br /> Ab - Majesty<br /> Ba - Dominate<br /> Ka - Protean<br /> Ren - Auspex<br /> Sheut - Nightmare<br /> <br /> Example: Seti is an Ashem with Sheut 5. He invests 4 points from any Pillar in Phobos, a Nosferatu elder with Blood Potency 7. Phobos has Nightmare 3. Thanks to the investment he has effectively Nightmare 8. This means he can access the powers of Nightmare 4 and 5 which he did not know before, and adds 8 dice for Nightmare to his dice pools to activate the discipline's powers rather than 3 only.<br /> <br /> Using Discipline powers beyond those already known to the vampire (like Nightmare 4 and 5 in the example) costs 1 Pillar point per scene, in addition to other normal costs.<br /> <br /> If the Arisen reincarnates in the invested vampire's body (let's say it's possible), what happens? I want to avoid a weird vampire-mummy hybrid. Is the Beast cast out? What does that look like? Or does the Arisen need to fight the Beast psychically before taking over?<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is for sure an interesting option but as a game master i would not recommend it, for two reasons:<br /> <br /> 1- Discipline levels are an expression of fine control on the Beast and Vitae power, Pillar points don t seem to heavily resonate with this.<br /> <br /> 2-&quot;Gifting&quot; free dots of something very costly in terms of experience seems too powerful considering the small investment by both the mummy and the vampire.<br /> <br /> From my experience, when designing those weird powers i would recommend those fundamentals:<br /> <br /> -The Decree Affinity is a main expression of the Mummy essence imposed on the cultist,it should always appear.<br /> <br /> -Human Sorcerer can use Pillars as substitute &quot;ingredients&quot; for Rituals, but Dark eras implies that as Pillars are the stuff of creation every kind of sorcery could benefit from them.<br /> Mages can use Pillars as Yantras.<br /> Vampires should absolutely use Pillars as Sacraments for appropriate blood sorcery rituals (if you use Theme rules you could associate each of them with a specific Pillar) and even devise special over the rules rituals that must use them.<br /> <br /> -Immortal and Sadiks are very compatible with Mummies powers, so it s natural that they benefit more from their Master power.<br /> Other creatures are less compatible, their benefits should be less powerful, also as a matter of balance<br /> <br /> -Benefits examples seems unrelated to the kind and quantity of Pillars invested, probably because they tend to change frequently and that limit eases book keeping.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For taking over Vampires cultist i would personally rule that while merging the character can use both Vampiric and Mummy powers (with the limits stated on the memory bleed conditions) but suffers both drawbacks.<br /> For added detail every time you spend willpower to unlock Utterances you could also lose access to a Discipline dot.<br /> After the fusion ends, the character is simply a Mummy with some memories and physical features of the ex vampire","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 09-10-2024, 08:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T05:03:26-07:00","id":1541850,"title":"","content":"Oh, and sin eaters should receive at least the twilight vision of the mummy, it would be very thematic and fun","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T20:02:43-07:00","id":1541909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1541723-ideas-on-how-supernaturals-respond-to-the-rite-of-investment?p=1541844#post1541844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is for sure an interesting option but as a game master i would not recommend it, for two reasons:<br /> <br /> 1- Discipline levels are an expression of fine control on the Beast and Vitae power, Pillar points don t seem to heavily resonate with this.<br /> <br /> 2-&quot;Gifting&quot; free dots of something very costly in terms of experience seems too powerful considering the small investment by both the mummy and the vampire.<br /> <br /> From my experience, when designing those weird powers i would recommend those fundamentals:<br /> <br /> -The Decree Affinity is a main expression of the Mummy essence imposed on the cultist,it should always appear.<br /> <br /> -Human Sorcerer can use Pillars as substitute &quot;ingredients&quot; for Rituals, but Dark eras implies that as Pillars are the stuff of creation every kind of sorcery could benefit from them.<br /> Mages can use Pillars as Yantras.<br /> Vampires should absolutely use Pillars as Sacraments for appropriate blood sorcery rituals (if you use Theme rules you could associate each of them with a specific Pillar) and even devise special over the rules rituals that must use them.<br /> <br /> -Immortal and Sadiks are very compatible with Mummies powers, so it s natural that they benefit more from their Master power.<br /> Other creatures are less compatible, their benefits should be less powerful, also as a matter of balance<br /> <br /> -Benefits examples seems unrelated to the kind and quantity of Pillars invested, probably because they tend to change frequently and that limit eases book keeping.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For taking over Vampires cultist i would personally rule that while merging the character can use both Vampiric and Mummy powers (with the limits stated on the memory bleed conditions) but suffers both drawbacks.<br /> For added detail every time you spend willpower to unlock Utterances you could also lose access to a Discipline dot.<br /> After the fusion ends, the character is simply a Mummy with some memories and physical features of the ex vampire</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are right in terms of power and cost. I probably got carried away by the idea of linking the five unique clan disciplines to the five Pillars, which <i>does work </i>pretty nicely correspondences wise.<br /> <br /> The Vitae could relate to the Pillars because it's a vehicle of Sekhem, as obvious by the Blood Bathers use for it and Shades craving it. But the issue is that Disciplines express both Vitae and the Beast, and I don't have a clear idea of how the Beast connects to the metaphysical underpinnings of the Arisen condition.<br /> <br /> I would prefer to avoid making Investment for vampires particulariy connected to Blood Sorcery, and I need to revise how Blood Sorcery works in 2e and how Pillars could enhance it or the other Covenant based Disciplines. At the same time, simply saying that Pillar Points can replace Vitae in fueling Disciplines seems not very attractive, as vampires can already hunt relatively easily, so it wouldn't be a significant boon.<br /> <br /> Aside from Mortal Decree (which ephemerals don't get though, and this is why I had excluded it at first) perhaps the simplest solution is to give them tier 1 Utterances like Immortals, but I'm not satisfied with that - too simplistic - and it removes the angle you mentioned for Blood Sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T23:24:44-07:00","id":1541915,"title":"","content":"Here's another attempt. I have revised Blood Sorcery, Mysteries of the Dragon, Carthian Law and Invictus Oaths, but I don't think the Pillars relate well enough to them. In a way, yes, as they all seem to stretch the vampire condition in one way or another, but not in a way relatable to the Arisen.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire Inheritors, second suggestion</b><br /> When looking at the effects of Investment on mortals, sorcerers, Sadikhs and Immortals, it seems clear that in all cases the Arisen's Defining Pillar is what grants the core boon (the Decree Affinity), while greater attunement to Sekhem leads to increasing ability to draw from the mummy's power. Which Pillars are invested makes no difference to a Mortal, Sadikh or Immortal except for the different feeling they give to the heart, while it's significant for Sorcerers because they spend specific Pillar points to lesser the requirements of rituals.<br /> <br /> With vampires, I don't want to use Mortal Decree because I want to show how different a vampire is, rather than just framing vampires as augmented mortals. I therefore present you with:<br /> <br /> <b>Vampiric Decree</b>: an Invested vampire feels the Arisen's Pillars tugging at the Vitae and the Beast from behind his heart. His soul now different from that of mortals, he instead filters the Mummy's Defining Pillar through the Beast, which sees new or latent potentialities in herself being brought out by the Investment.<br /> <br /> Depending on the Arisen's Defining Pillar, the vampire becomes able to learn a new Discipline without needing to imbibe first Vitae from someone who knows it. Should he have already imbibed such and gained access to the Discipline, he may now purchase new dots at in-clan cost rather than out-of-clan. Should it be already a Clan dicipline for him, he can spend a Pillar point to gain bonus dice equal to the Arisen's master dots in his Defining Pillar on a single activation roll.<br /> <br /> The Pillar-Discipline combinations are:<br /> <br /> Ab-Majesty<br /> Ba - Dominate<br /> Ka - Protean<br /> Ren - Auspex<br /> Sheut - Nightmare.<br /> <br /> A vampire can store a number of Pillar points equal to his Blood Potency divided by 3 and rounded up, hence:<br /> <br /> BP 1-3 = 1 point<br /> 4-6=2<br /> 7-9=3<br /> 10=4","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-11T08:47:22-07:00","id":1541925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1541723-ideas-on-how-supernaturals-respond-to-the-rite-of-investment?p=1541915#post1541915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's another attempt. I have revised Blood Sorcery, Mysteries of the Dragon, Carthian Law and Invictus Oaths, but I don't think the Pillars relate well enough to them. In a way, yes, as they all seem to stretch the vampire condition in one way or another, but not in a way relatable to the Arisen.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire Inheritors, second suggestion</b><br /> When looking at the effects of Investment on mortals, sorcerers, Sadikhs and Immortals, it seems clear that in all cases the Arisen's Defining Pillar is what grants the core boon (the Decree Affinity), while greater attunement to Sekhem leads to increasing ability to draw from the mummy's power. Which Pillars are invested makes no difference to a Mortal, Sadikh or Immortal except for the different feeling they give to the heart, while it's significant for Sorcerers because they spend specific Pillar points to lesser the requirements of rituals.<br /> <br /> With vampires, I don't want to use Mortal Decree because I want to show how different a vampire is, rather than just framing vampires as augmented mortals. I therefore present you with:<br /> <br /> <b>Vampiric Decree</b>: an Invested vampire feels the Arisen's Pillars tugging at the Vitae and the Beast from behind his heart. His soul now different from that of mortals, he instead filters the Mummy's Defining Pillar through the Beast, which sees new or latent potentialities in herself being brought out by the Investment.<br /> <br /> Depending on the Arisen's Defining Pillar, the vampire becomes able to learn a new Discipline without needing to imbibe first Vitae from someone who knows it. Should he have already imbibed such and gained access to the Discipline, he may now purchase new dots at in-clan cost rather than out-of-clan. Should it be already a Clan dicipline for him, he can spend a Pillar point to gain bonus dice equal to the Arisen's master dots in his Defining Pillar on a single activation roll.<br /> <br /> The Pillar-Discipline combinations are:<br /> <br /> Ab-Majesty<br /> Ba - Dominate<br /> Ka - Protean<br /> Ren - Auspex<br /> Sheut - Nightmare.<br /> <br /> A vampire can store a number of Pillar points equal to his Blood Potency divided by 3 and rounded up, hence:<br /> <br /> BP 1-3 = 1 point<br /> 4-6=2<br /> 7-9=3<br /> 10=4</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it.<br /> As an add on or alternative i would suggest this:<br /> Whenever a Vampire inheritor uses Phisical intensity he can spend a Pillar dot to boost the buff duration for a whole scene (not cumulable)<br /> What do you say?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-11T22:17:17-07:00","id":1541951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1541723-ideas-on-how-supernaturals-respond-to-the-rite-of-investment?p=1541925#post1541925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like it.<br /> As an add on or alternative i would suggest this:<br /> Whenever a Vampire inheritor uses Phisical intensity he can spend a Pillar dot to boost the buff duration for a whole scene (not cumulable)<br /> What do you say?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a good idea to give something out of the Investment also to physical vampire characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T12:26:17-07:00","id":1541979,"title":"","content":"Hi, I'm just popping in here to let you both know that there actually <i>is</i> a canon answer for what happens when a mummy invests a Pillar into a vampire. It's on p. 349 of <b>Dark Eras 2</b> in blink-and-you'll-miss-it section of the Reign of Terror chapter.<br /> <br /> Basically, a mummy who attempts to invest a Pillar point into a vampire <i>loses that entire Pillar</i> until their next Descent [or after? The wording is a little funny]. Obviously, this isn't very conducive to the kind of game you're imagining, and even the [very] soft implication in the same section that vampires would be invested like other immortals if they didn't eat it isn't really helpful either. Especially since you've just finished coming up with an answer that works <i>much better</i> for your purposes lol.<br /> <br /> Still, I thought you might like to know about it, if only as a bit of trivia or another example of what can happen as a result of investment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T13:39:47-07:00","id":1541984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SomethingFishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1541723-ideas-on-how-supernaturals-respond-to-the-rite-of-investment?p=1541979#post1541979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, I'm just popping in here to let you both know that there actually <i>is</i> a canon answer for what happens when a mummy invests a Pillar into a vampire. It's on p. 349 of <b>Dark Eras 2</b> in blink-and-you'll-miss-it section of the Reign of Terror chapter.<br /> <br /> Basically, a mummy who attempts to invest a Pillar point into a vampire <i>loses that entire Pillar</i> until their next Descent [or after? The wording is a little funny]. Obviously, this isn't very conducive to the kind of game you're imagining, and even the [very] soft implication in the same section that vampires would be invested like other immortals if they didn't eat it isn't really helpful either. Especially since you've just finished coming up with an answer that works <i>much better</i> for your purposes lol.<br /> <br /> Still, I thought you might like to know about it, if only as a bit of trivia or another example of what can happen as a result of investment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh thank you!<br /> <br /> It really looks like I need to read Dark Eras 2, it keeps being mentioned in the discussions I join.<br /> <br /> Does it give a reason <i>why</i> investing a Pillar would do that? Does the vampire/Beast somehow steal the Pillar like some kind of metaphysical vitae? Or is it a punishment from the Judges for some reason?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T14:45:37-07:00","id":1541995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1541723-ideas-on-how-supernaturals-respond-to-the-rite-of-investment?p=1541984#post1541984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it give a reason <i>why</i> investing a Pillar would do that? Does the vampire/Beast somehow steal the Pillar like some kind of metaphysical vitae? Or is it a punishment from the Judges for some reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>It leaves it an open question, but says some Arisen theorize vampires are bastard &quot;children&quot; of the Devourer and can't help but metaphysically consume the Pillar. Whether or not that's true is up to individual tables, of course.<br /> But it looks a little like diablerie to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T15:54:17-07:00","id":1542004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SomethingFishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1541723-ideas-on-how-supernaturals-respond-to-the-rite-of-investment?p=1541995#post1541995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It leaves it an open question, but says some Arisen theorize vampires are bastard &quot;children&quot; of the Devourer and can't help but metaphysically consume the Pillar. Whether or not that's true is up to individual tables, of course.<br /> But it looks a little like diablerie to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's quite interesting actually.<br /> <br /> What other Mummy crossover mechanics are covered in Dark Eras 2? So far I heard of what you just mentioned + Promethean Universal Milestones/Arisen Pillars + something about Mage Arcana / Arisen Pillars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T20:25:21-07:00","id":1542015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1541723-ideas-on-how-supernaturals-respond-to-the-rite-of-investment?p=1542004#post1542004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What other Mummy crossover mechanics are covered in Dark Eras 2? So far I heard of what you just mentioned + Promethean Universal Milestones/Arisen Pillars + something about Mage Arcana / Arisen Pillars.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Promethean bit isn't mechanics; the sidebar Neos mentioned is in the Promethean/Beast/Werewolf Dark Era set in Egypt at the end of the Middle Kingdom, which tilts the way local Created theorize on the metaphysics of the Pilgrimage in ways whose nomenclature overlaps with the Pillars because they're referring to the same parts of the soul.<br /> <br /> The Mage/Mummy material is in the &quot;Crossover in the Conquered Land&quot; section of the Dark Eras Companion's &quot;Princes of the Conquered Land&quot; Era set in the Mutapa Empire in the 16th Century, which addresses things like reconciling the Arisen's perspective on Twilight as a place with the Awakened view of it as a series of states, how the Subtle Arcana correlate to the Pillars of the fivefold soul, and what Mana and Pillars can do with the magical items of mummies and mages respectively.<br /> <br /> <br /> A suggestion for werewolves that might be a bit too out-there, depending on your game, is that an Invested werewolf gains an appropriate enlightenment \u2014 powers attributed to legendary werewolves and more commonly found in the hands of the Ghost Wolves known as devourers, who maintain them through ritual cannibalism of other werewolves (detailed in Night Horrors: Shunned by the Moon) \u2014 substituting the Arisen's rating in that Pillar for the relevant Renown where applicable for as long as they retain that Pillar.<br /> <br /> Invested deviants might gain the benefits of being a Guardian (or Nemesis) more easily, treating their Loyalty (or Conviction) rating as one higher for the purposes of achieving Catharsis (or Fury) at the cost of treating defying their Arisen master's commands as a trigger for Faltering even if they don't hold them as a Loyalty Touchstone.<br /> <br /> Invested demons may be able to spend their Pillars as Cover Experiences to create a more stable mortal identity at the cost of being Flagged for the mummy and their cultists instead of the God-Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T23:20:28-07:00","id":1542029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1541723-ideas-on-how-supernaturals-respond-to-the-rite-of-investment?p=1542015#post1542015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Promethean bit isn't mechanics; the sidebar Neos mentioned is in the Promethean/Beast/Werewolf Dark Era set in Egypt at the end of the Middle Kingdom, which tilts the way local Created theorize on the metaphysics of the Pilgrimage in ways whose nomenclature overlaps with the Pillars because they're referring to the same parts of the soul.<br /> <br /> The Mage/Mummy material is in the &quot;Crossover in the Conquered Land&quot; section of the Dark Eras Companion's &quot;Princes of the Conquered Land&quot; Era set in the Mutapa Empire in the 16th Century, which addresses things like reconciling the Arisen's perspective on Twilight as a place with the Awakened view of it as a series of states, how the Subtle Arcana correlate to the Pillars of the fivefold soul, and what Mana and Pillars can do with the magical items of mummies and mages respectively.<br /> <br /> <br /> A suggestion for werewolves that might be a bit too out-there, depending on your game, is that an Invested werewolf gains an appropriate enlightenment \u2014 powers attributed to legendary werewolves and more commonly found in the hands of the Ghost Wolves known as devourers, who maintain them through ritual cannibalism of other werewolves (detailed in Night Horrors: Shunned by the Moon) \u2014 substituting the Arisen's rating in that Pillar for the relevant Renown where applicable for as long as they retain that Pillar.<br /> <br /> Invested deviants might gain the benefits of being a Guardian (or Nemesis) more easily, treating their Loyalty (or Conviction) rating as one higher for the purposes of achieving Catharsis (or Fury) at the cost of treating defying their Arisen master's commands as a trigger for Faltering even if they don't hold them as a Loyalty Touchstone.<br /> <br /> Invested demons may be able to spend their Pillars as Cover Experiences to create a more stable mortal identity at the cost of being Flagged for the mummy and their cultists instead of the God-Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}